<title>SPAIN: PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</title>
<headline>PESETA DEBT/INTERBANK CLOSING REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds slid into the close on Wednesday but managed to crawl off lows after a volatile session battered by a bout of mixed data, dealers said.</p>
<p>Thursday's session is expected to be quiet ahead of a national holiday in Spain and Italy on Friday.</p>
<p>Bonds assumed a negative tone in early trade after disappointing Spanish July CPI data which rose 0.2 percent month-on-month and was unchanged at 1.6 percent year-on-year. The core rate was a higher-than-expected 2.0 percent year-on-year versus 1.9 percent in June.</p>
</text>
